@page "/customer-portal/terms"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@layout CustomerPortalLayout

<PageTitle>Terms of Service - Customer Portal</PageTitle>

@* The sibling of CustomerPrivacy.razor, on the same `cpd` blocks — see the
   note at the top of that file. The terms text is unchanged; only the markup
   carrying it is. *@
<div class="cpd fade-in">
    <div class="cpd-hero">
        <div class="cpd-hero-text">
            <h2>Terms of Service</h2>
            <div class="cpd-hero-meta">
                <span>The terms governing your use of the Customer Portal</span>
                <span>Last updated March 2026</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cpd-hero-actions">
            <a href="/customer-portal/privacy" class="btn btn-outline-primary">Privacy policy</a>
            <a href="/customer-portal/support" class="btn btn-primary">Contact support</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cpd-note">
        <i class="ph ph-info" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span>
            This portal is operated in compliance with the Postal and Telecommunications Regulatory
            Authority of Zimbabwe (POTRAZ) regulations and the Cyber and Data Protection Act
            [Chapter 12:07] of Zimbabwe.
        </span>
    </div>

    <div class="cpd-panel">
        <div class="cpd-stamp">Last updated: March 2026</div>

        <div class="cpd-prose">
            <h3>1. Acceptance of Terms</h3>
            <p>
                By accessing and using the Customer Portal, you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service,
                the laws of Zimbabwe, and all applicable regulations issued by the Postal and Telecommunications
                Regulatory Authority of Zimbabwe (POTRAZ). If you do not agree to these terms, you should not
                use the portal.
            </p>

            <h3>2. Regulatory Framework</h3>
            <p>
                This portal and the services provided through it are governed by the following Zimbabwean legislation
                and regulatory instruments:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>The Cyber and Data Protection Act [Chapter 12:07] (2021)</li>
                <li>The Postal and Telecommunications Act [Chapter 12:05]</li>
                <li>POTRAZ Consumer Protection Regulations</li>
                <li>SI 160 of 2021 — Cyber and Data Protection (General) Regulations</li>
                <li>The Electronic Transactions and Electronic Commerce Act [Chapter 21:20]</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>3. Account Access</h3>
            <p>
                You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your login credentials. You agree to
                notify us immediately of any unauthorised use of your account. We reserve the right to suspend
                or terminate access to accounts that violate these terms or applicable POTRAZ regulations.
            </p>

            <h3>4. Permitted Use</h3>
            <p>The Customer Portal is provided for the purpose of:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Viewing and downloading account statements and invoices</li>
                <li>Making payments against outstanding invoices</li>
                <li>Managing your account profile and contact details</li>
                <li>Submitting support requests</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>5. Prohibited Activities</h3>
            <p>You agree not to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to other accounts or system resources</li>
                <li>Use automated tools to scrape or extract data from the portal</li>
                <li>Interfere with the proper functioning of the portal</li>
                <li>Use the portal for any unlawful purpose or in violation of POTRAZ regulations</li>
                <li>
                    Transmit or distribute harmful digital content as defined under the Cyber and Data
                    Protection Act
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h3>6. Payment Terms</h3>
            <p>
                Payments made through the Customer Portal are subject to the payment terms agreed in your
                commercial contract. All transactions are processed securely in compliance with POTRAZ
                requirements for electronic commerce. Payment confirmations will be provided upon successful
                processing. All electronic transaction records are maintained as required by the Electronic
                Transactions and Electronic Commerce Act.
            </p>

            <h3>7. Data Protection and Privacy</h3>
            <p>
                In accordance with the Cyber and Data Protection Act [Chapter 12:07] and POTRAZ data protection
                requirements:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    We process your personal data only for lawful purposes and with your consent as required
                    under Section 8 of the Act
                </li>
                <li>
                    Your personal data is stored and processed within Zimbabwe or in jurisdictions that provide
                    adequate data protection as determined by the Data Protection Authority
                </li>
                <li>
                    We do not transfer your personal data outside Zimbabwe without ensuring compliance with
                    Section 29 of the Act (cross-border transfer provisions)
                </li>
                <li>
                    You have the right to access, correct, and request deletion of your personal data as provided
                    under Sections 22–28 of the Act
                </li>
                <li>
                    We maintain appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect your data as required
                    by POTRAZ security standards
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                For full details on how we handle your data, please refer to our
                <a href="/customer-portal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
            </p>

            <h3>8. Data Subject Rights</h3>
            <p>Under the Cyber and Data Protection Act, as a data subject you are entitled to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Be informed about the collection and use of your personal data</li>
                <li>Access your personal data held by us</li>
                <li>Request rectification of inaccurate or incomplete personal data</li>
                <li>
                    Request erasure of your personal data where there is no compelling reason for continued
                    processing
                </li>
                <li>Object to the processing of your personal data</li>
                <li>Data portability — receive your data in a structured, commonly used format</li>
                <li>
                    Lodge a complaint with the Data Protection Authority of Zimbabwe if you believe your rights
                    have been violated
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h3>9. Data Breach Notification</h3>
            <p>
                In the event of a personal data breach that poses a risk to your rights and freedoms, we will
                notify the Data Protection Authority within 72 hours of becoming aware of the breach, in
                accordance with Section 30 of the Cyber and Data Protection Act. Where the breach is likely to
                result in a high risk to you, we will also notify you directly without undue delay.
            </p>

            <h3>10. Consumer Protection</h3>
            <p>In compliance with POTRAZ consumer protection regulations, we commit to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Providing clear and transparent information about our services and pricing</li>
                <li>Maintaining a fair and accessible complaints handling procedure</li>
                <li>Responding to complaints within timeframes prescribed by POTRAZ</li>
                <li>Not engaging in unfair business practices or misleading conduct</li>
                <li>Providing you with the right to escalate unresolved complaints to POTRAZ</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>11. Complaints and Dispute Resolution</h3>
            <p>If you have a complaint about our services:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>Step 1:</strong> Contact us through the
                    <a href="/customer-portal/support">Support</a> page. We will acknowledge your complaint
                    within 2 business days and aim to resolve it within 14 business days.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Step 2:</strong> If you are not satisfied with our response, you may escalate your
                    complaint to POTRAZ at: Postal and Telecommunications Regulatory Authority of Zimbabwe,
                    Block A, Emerald Business Park, 30 The Chase (West), P.O. Box MP 843, Mount Pleasant,
                    Harare, Zimbabwe.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Step 3:</strong> For data protection matters, you may lodge a complaint with the
                    Data Protection Authority established under the Cyber and Data Protection Act.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h3>12. Data Accuracy</h3>
            <p>
                While we strive to ensure the accuracy of all information displayed on the portal, including
                invoice amounts and statement balances, the data is synchronised from our business systems and
                may occasionally be subject to processing delays. In case of any discrepancy, the records in
                our core business system shall prevail.
            </p>

            <h3>13. Service Availability</h3>
            <p>
                We aim to provide continuous access to the Customer Portal, however, we do not guarantee
                uninterrupted availability. The portal may be temporarily unavailable due to maintenance,
                updates, or circumstances beyond our control. Service interruptions will be communicated
                where practicable in accordance with POTRAZ service quality standards.
            </p>

            <h3>14. Limitation of Liability</h3>
            <p>
                To the fullest extent permitted by the laws of Zimbabwe, we shall not be liable for any indirect,
                incidental, or consequential damages arising from the use of the Customer Portal. Our total
                liability shall not exceed the value of the transactions in dispute. Nothing in these terms
                excludes or limits liability that cannot be excluded under Zimbabwean law.
            </p>

            <h3>15. Governing Law and Jurisdiction</h3>
            <p>
                These Terms of Service are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of Zimbabwe.
                Any disputes arising from the use of this portal shall be subject to the jurisdiction of the
                courts of Zimbabwe. Regulatory matters fall under the jurisdiction of POTRAZ as established
                by the Postal and Telecommunications Act [Chapter 12:05].
            </p>

            <h3>16. Changes to Terms</h3>
            <p>
                We reserve the right to modify these Terms of Service at any time in accordance with applicable
                law and POTRAZ regulations. Material changes will be communicated to you via the portal or
                email. Continued use of the portal after changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the
                revised terms.
            </p>

            <h3>17. Contact</h3>
            <p>
                For questions about these terms, please reach out via the
                <a href="/customer-portal/support">Support</a> page.
            </p>
            <p class="cpd-stamp">
                Regulatory enquiries may be directed to POTRAZ at
                <a href="https://www.potraz.gov.zw" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.potraz.gov.zw</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
